 Mercurial, Bazaar and CVS tests skip when their binaries are missing, and LDAP tests skip without an LDAP server.\n- Finding: on a new SQLite3 database, `bin/rails db:prepare` fails every time at migration 072 (`db/migrate/072_add_enumerations_position.rb`) with `no such column: enumerations.position`. The migration skips `add_column` when `Enumeration.column_names` already lists `position`, so stale column information makes it fail. `bin/rails db:create db:migrate` passes every time (CI uses it too, through `ci:setup`). `bin/harness setup` therefore uses `db:create db:migrate`. The migration was not changed; a human should decide whether to fix it upstream.\n- `.tool-versions` pins Ruby 4.0.0 (the version the gates were verified with, also in the CI matrix) and Node.js 20 (the CI version). `.ruby-version` is ignored by git upstream, so it was not used.\n\n## 2026-11-01: harness built by uw-harness 0.3.0 with claude\n\nScore 19 → 92, level 0 → 2.\n\nThe harness uses Rake, the task runner Redmine already has: new tasks in the root Rakefile, plus a bin/harness wrapper that picks a supported Ruby and bootstraps config/database.yml for SQLite3 before bundle install. From a clean shell, `bin/harness setup` works. `bin/harness check-fast` passes in about 40 s (RuboCop, Stylelint, 3383 unit and helper tests, 0 failures). `bin/harness check` passes in about 3 minutes (6296 tests plus the autoload test, 0 failures). No test was skipped, deleted or excluded, and no product code changed. One finding: `db:prepare` always fails at migration 072 on a new database, so setup uses `db:create db:migrate`. Docs, three ADRs (two inferred), four skills, AGENTS.md, a CI workflow running uw-harness verify, a pre-push hook, compose.yaml, .env.example and .tool-versions were added. Seven open questions (deploy, observability, contribution process, CI, default database, skipped tests) are TODO blocks.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_me